#
# rsyslog takes log lines from this box only, not from the network.
#
# The production package set ships rsyslog with its UDP input on port 514,
# listening on every address - br-lan included, which is the same L2 domain
# as every client of the mesh. Nothing of ours sends to it: no box has a
# remote log target set, and the mesh reads its logs from /var/log/messages
# of the box itself (easymesh-logkeep, the events API). What it did offer is
# a way for anyone on the LAN to write lines into that file - which lives in
# RAM and which our tools read as the truth. Measured 2026-09-30 on every lab
# box: rsyslogd bound to 0.0.0.0:514 and :::514.
#
# Local logging (imuxsock, /var/log/messages) is untouched; see
# 93-easymesh-single-kmsg-reader for why the kernel log is not read here.

[ -f /etc/config/rsyslog ] || exit 0
[ "$(uci -q get rsyslog.syslog.udp_input)" = 1 ] || exit 0

uci set rsyslog.syslog.udp_input='0'
uci commit rsyslog

# Only if it is already running - at first boot the init system has not
# started it yet and this would race with that.
[ -n "$(pidof rsyslogd)" ] && /etc/init.d/rsyslog restart >/dev/null 2>&1

exit 0
